{
 "texts": {
  "frontMatter/0": "EXECUTION VERSION – Confidential",
  "body/0": "AGREEMENT AND PLAN OF MERGER (this “Agreement”), dated as of May 1, 2024, among Alpha & Omega Holdings, Inc., a Delaware corporation (“Parent”), and Beta Corp. 𝔅 Ltd., a Delaware corporation (the “Company”).",
  "body/1": "WHEREAS, the parties intend the merger to qualify under § 368(a) of the Code, as described in Section 1.1 and Section 2.1(b);",
  "art-1/0": "This Article I applies to the “Company” and to Parent.",
  "sec-1-1/0": "(a) “Business Day” means any day other than a Saturday — or Sunday — on which banks in New York are open; “Closing” has the meaning set forth in Section 2.1.",
  "sec-1-1/1": "“Material Adverse Effect” means any change that is material to the Company 𝔅 & its Subsidiaries, see Section 2.1(b).",
  "sec-1-1/2": "(b) Each Business Day of the Company is a “Trading Day”.",
  "art-1/1": "Text in a section without a uuid stays in the article container; the Closing occurs on a Business Day.",
  "sec-2-1/0": "(a) The Closing shall take place on the second Business Day after the conditions in Section 1.1 are satisfied.",
  "sec-2-1/1": "(b) At the Closing, the Company and Parent shall deliver the documents described in Section 2.1(a).",
  "backMatter/0": "Exhibit A – Form of Certificate; the Company’s charter, Section 1.1."
 },
